## Why the split

Teams building regulated health software quote design guidance verbatim inside
clinical-safety cases, hazard logs and design-history files. CC BY 4.0 gives them an
unambiguous right to do that, with an attribution requirement rather than a
share-alike obligation that would infect their internal documents. MIT alone is a
software licence and says nothing useful about copying prose into a PDF that goes to
a regulator.

## Attributing it

> Adapted from the opsinjs documentation (https://opsinjs.pensievelabs.org), CC BY 4.0.

Include the page title and, where the guidance is dated or under review, the
`reviewed` date printed at the foot of the page. If you have modified the guidance,
say so. A reviewer must be able to tell your rule from ours.

